# AGENTS.md

Instructions for coding agents working on {{ title }}, a multi-tenant Navree
app from the `{{ kit }}` starter kit: a Rust API built from modules wired by
dependency injection{% if web %}, and a Next.js front end in `web/` that
reaches it through its own server (a backend-for-frontend){% endif %}. Read
this file before changing code.

## Layout

```text
config/app.toml        settings shared by every environment (committed)
.env                   this machine's secrets and Dock's settings (never committed)
dock.toml              local services: `navree dock up` (PostgreSQL, Mailpit)
harbor.toml            servers and deploys: `navree deploy`
src/main.rs            runs the app: `serve` by default, or any other command
src/app.rs             the root: platform() plus the feature modules
src/platform.rs        the framework modules, configured once
src/abilities.rs       who may do what: permissions and ability rules
src/seed.rs            the demo workspace (`navree migrate:fresh --seed`)
src/modules/<name>/    feature modules: accounts, settings, projects, admin
tests/                 tests that boot the whole app on a fresh database
{% if web %}
web/                   the Next.js front end; its server holds the API tokens
{% endif %}
```

## Commands

```sh
navree dock up                              # PostgreSQL and Mailpit in containers
navree dev                                  # API on :8080{% if web %}, web app on :3000{% endif %}, rebuild on save
cargo test                                  # every test; each boots the app on its own SQLite database
cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings   # must pass
cargo fmt                                   # must leave nothing to change
navree check                                # validate the module graph without booting
navree routes                               # every route with its access rule
navree migrate:fresh --seed                 # rebuild the database with the demo data
navree openapi:export openapi.json          # the API contract, committed and checked in CI
{% if web %}
pnpm --dir web test                         # the backend-for-frontend's unit tests
pnpm --dir web build                        # type check and build the front end
{% endif %}
```

The demo accounts are `owner@{{ package | replace("_", "-") }}.test` (also a super admin, for
`/admin`) and `member@{{ package | replace("_", "-") }}.test`, password `password123`, in the
workspace `demo`.

## Workspaces come first

Every product route belongs to a workspace. Copy the shape of
`src/modules/projects/`:

- the entity has a `workspace_id` column and implements `Subject` and
  `WorkspaceScoped`; its migration runs `.after(["workspace"])` and adds the
  PostgreSQL row-level security policy (`RlsPolicy::new("<table>")`);
- the module registers `m.workspace_scoped::<Entity>()` and imports
  `AccessModule::for_feature::<Entity>()`;
- the controller has `#[guard(InWorkspace::guard())]`, takes
  `CurrentWorkspace` and `WorkspaceUow`, and declares access per route with
  `#[can(Action, Subject)]` (`from = "id"` loads the record: another
  workspace's is a 404);
- the service reads and writes through `WorkspaceRepo::<Entity>` only.

The workspace comes from the `X-Workspace` header (its slug or id). Grant
each workspace role its permissions in `config/app.toml`
(`[workspace.roles.member] permissions = ["projects.read", ...]`); add
conditional rules in `src/abilities.rs`.

## Generate code, then fill it in

Use the generators: they follow the conventions and register what they
create at the marker comments `// navree:modules` (src/app.rs),
`// navree:wire` (a module's `wire`) and `// navree:policies`
(src/abilities.rs). Keep those markers. Names are snake_case; module names
are plural. Generators never overwrite a file.

| To add | Run |
|---|---|
| A feature module (then make it workspace-scoped like `projects/`) | `navree make:module invoices --crud` |
| A migration | `navree make:migration invoices add_due_date_to_invoices` |
| A queued job | `navree make:job invoices send_reminder` |
| An event and a listener | `navree make:event invoices invoice_paid`, then `navree make:listener invoices notify_owner --event invoice_paid` |
| A mail | `navree make:mail invoices overdue` |
| An admin-panel resource | `navree make:resource invoices Invoice` |
| A test | `navree make:test invoices reminders` |

## Conventions

- **Deny by default.** Every route declares who may call it with
  `#[public]`, `#[authenticated]`, `#[roles(..)]`, `#[permissions(..)]` or
  `#[can(Action, Subject)]`. Never make a route `#[public]` to get past a
  401 or a 403: grant the permission or add an ability rule.
- **Input.** Request bodies are DTOs deriving `Deserialize`,
  `garde::Validate` and `utoipa::ToSchema`; handlers take
  `Valid(Json(input)): Valid<Json<T>>`, and declare `#[api(..)]` so the
  OpenAPI document{% if web %} (and the front end's generated client){% endif %} stays exact.
- **Errors.** Handlers return `Result<T>` (`AppError`): `AppError::not_found()`,
  `AppError::forbidden()`, `AppError::bad_request("..")`,
  `AppError::conflict("..").with_code("..")`. Every error response is
  `{ "statusCode", "message", "error", "code" }`.
- **Database.** SeaORM entities with UUID v7 ids; writes take the request's
  unit of work first and go through `Repo` / `WorkspaceRepo` (audited);
  lists take `PageQuery` and return `Page<T>`.
- **Migrations** belong to their module's `MigrationSet`; never edit one
  that has run anywhere, add a new one.
- **Configuration.** `config/app.toml` holds shared settings; secrets go in
  `.env` or the environment (`APP_BILLING__STRIPE__SECRET_KEY`).
- **Tests.** Every change comes with tests. `tests/support/mod.rs` boots the
  app with the committed `config/app.toml` on a fresh database and has
  helpers for accounts, sign-in and workspaces.
{% if web %}
- **Front end.** The browser calls only the web app's own routes;
  `web/lib/bff` forwards them to the API with the bearer token from an
  httpOnly cookie. Never put a token in browser storage. After changing a
  DTO, run `navree openapi:export web/openapi.json` and `pnpm --dir web gen:api`.
{% endif %}

## Before you finish

Run `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` and
`cargo test`{% if web %}, and `pnpm --dir web lint`, `pnpm --dir web test` and
`pnpm --dir web build`{% endif %}, and fix everything they report.

